From c6e5877e05ba8030172e42d78a6b38f3c3e954b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 18:53:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] fix: installer produced a stack that could not boot

install.sh wrote APP_ENV=production together with a blank COMP_LENS_API_KEYS,
and the lifespan guard in app/main.py refuses to start in production when no
API keys are configured. The documented one-command install therefore always
ended at 'App did not report healthy within 3 minutes'.

Reproduced with the installer's exact .env values:
  RuntimeError: Refusing to start: APP_ENV=production but no API keys are
  configured. Set COMP_LENS_API_KEYS to enable authentication.

The installer now mints an admin key, writes it as '<key>:*', prints it with a
ready-to-paste curl example, and fails fast with a clear message if an existing
.env has APP_ENV=production and no key. docker-compose promotes the same
variable to a required one (:?) so the failure surfaces at 'up' rather than in
a health-check timeout. It also stopped advertising /docs, which is disabled in
production; EXPOSE_API_DOCS is now plumbed through for anyone who wants it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BX61MEYft2zHyTikPWZeGG
---
 .env.example       | 15 ++++++++++++---
 DEPLOY.md          | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++----
 docker-compose.yml |  6 +++++-
 install.sh         | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 4 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.env.example b/.env.example
index 0d1af81..e6f8e30 100644
--- a/.env.example
+++ b/.env.example
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 # Comp-Lens configuration — copy to .env, or just run ./install.sh to generate it.
-# The installer fills POSTGRES_PASSWORD and EVIDENCE_SIGNING_KEY with random secrets.
+# The installer fills POSTGRES_PASSWORD, EVIDENCE_SIGNING_KEY and COMP_LENS_API_KEYS
+# with random secrets. If you write this file by hand, all three are REQUIRED when
+# APP_ENV=production — the app fails closed and refuses to boot without them.
 
 POSTGRES_USER=complens
 POSTGRES_PASSWORD=          # auto-generated by install.sh
@@ -12,8 +14,15 @@ HOST_PORT=8000
 ENABLE_SCHEDULER=false
 EVIDENCE_BACKEND=local
 
-# Optional API auth — blank = no auth. Format: "key:tenant,key2:*"
-COMP_LENS_API_KEYS=
+# Interactive API docs (/docs, /redoc). Off in production by default because they
+# disclose the full API surface. Set true if you want them exposed anyway.
+EXPOSE_API_DOCS=false
+
+# API auth — REQUIRED when APP_ENV=production. Blank means "no auth", which would
+# make every caller an all-tenant admin, so the app refuses to start instead.
+# Format: "key:tenant,key2:*"  —  ':*' grants access to every tenant; separate
+# multiple entries with ';'. Generate a key with:  openssl rand -hex 32
+COMP_LENS_API_KEYS=         # auto-generated by install.sh, e.g. 3f9a…:*
 
 # Optional — which connectors make live API calls. e.g. OKTA,GITHUB,AWS
 LIVE_CONNECTORS_ALLOWLIST=
diff --git a/DEPLOY.md b/DEPLOY.md
index a6a466c..3a3f1c9 100644
--- a/DEPLOY.md
+++ b/DEPLOY.md
@@ -3,21 +3,38 @@
 One command. On any Linux server with Docker installed:
 
 ```bash
-git clone https://github.com/shalak97/Comp-lens-2.0.git
-cd Comp-lens-2.0
+git clone https://github.com/shalak97/Comp-lens.git
+cd Comp-lens
 ./install.sh
 ```
 
 The installer:
 1. Checks Docker + Compose are present
-2. Generates a random database password and evidence signing key
+2. Generates a random database password, evidence signing key, and admin API key
 3. Writes them to `.env` (mode 600, gitignored — never committed)
 4. Builds the app image and starts the app + PostgreSQL
 5. Runs database migrations automatically
-6. Waits until the app reports healthy, then prints your dashboard URL
+6. Waits until the app reports healthy, then prints your dashboard URL and API key
 
 When it finishes you'll have Comp-Lens at `http://your-server:8000/dashboard`.
 
+## Authentication
+
+The stack runs with `APP_ENV=production`, which makes the app fail closed: it
+refuses to start unless both `COMP_LENS_API_KEYS` and `EVIDENCE_SIGNING_KEY` are
+set. `install.sh` generates both. Send the admin key on every API call:
+
+```bash
+curl -H "X-API-Key: $YOUR_KEY" http://your-server:8000/summary
+```
+
+Keys are tenant-scoped: `key:acme,globex` limits a key to those two tenants and
+`key:*` grants access to all of them. Separate multiple entries with `;`.
+
+Interactive API docs (`/docs`, `/redoc`) are off in production so the API surface
+isn't disclosed to anonymous callers. Set `EXPOSE_API_DOCS=true` in `.env` and
+re-run `./install.sh` if you want them.
+
 ## Day-two operations
 
 ```bash
diff --git a/docker-compose.yml b/docker-compose.yml
index 04be868..73f95d4 100644
--- a/docker-compose.yml
+++ b/docker-compose.yml
@@ -40,9 +40,13 @@ services:
       AUTO_CREATE_TABLES: "false"
       ENABLE_SCHEDULER: ${ENABLE_SCHEDULER:-false}
       POLICY_DIR: /app/policies
+      ENFORCEMENT_POLICY_DIR: /app/enforcement_policy
       EVIDENCE_BACKEND: ${EVIDENCE_BACKEND:-local}
       EVIDENCE_LOCAL_PATH: /data/evidence
-      COMP_LENS_API_KEYS: ${COMP_LENS_API_KEYS:-}
+      EXPOSE_API_DOCS: ${EXPOSE_API_DOCS:-false}
+      # Required when APP_ENV=production: the app fails closed and refuses to
+      # boot without a key, because a blank value makes every caller an admin.
+      COMP_LENS_API_KEYS: ${COMP_LENS_API_KEYS:?set COMP_LENS_API_KEYS in .env, e.g. "<key>:*" — run ./install.sh to generate one}
       LIVE_CONNECTORS_ALLOWLIST: ${LIVE_CONNECTORS_ALLOWLIST:-}
       # connector credentials pass through from .env (uncomment in .env as needed)
       OKTA_ORG_URL: ${OKTA_ORG_URL:-}
diff --git a/install.sh b/install.sh
index c56d23f..87dd1fe 100755
--- a/install.sh
+++ b/install.sh
@@ -63,6 +63,11 @@ else
   info "Generating secrets and writing $ENV_FILE…"
   SIGNING_KEY="$(gen_secret)"
   DB_PASS="$(gen_secret | cut -c1-24)"
+  # APP_ENV=production makes the app fail closed: it refuses to boot unless an
+  # API key is configured (otherwise every caller would be an all-tenant admin).
+  # So the installer must mint one — a blank COMP_LENS_API_KEYS here would leave
+  # the stack permanently unhealthy.
+  ADMIN_KEY="$(gen_secret)"
   cat > "$ENV_FILE" <<ENVEOF
 # ─── Comp-Lens configuration (generated $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%MZ)) ───
 # Secrets below were auto-generated. Keep this file private — do NOT commit it.
@@ -81,9 +86,11 @@ HOST_PORT=${HOST_PORT}
 ENABLE_SCHEDULER=false
 EVIDENCE_BACKEND=local
 
-# ─── Optional: API auth ───────────────────────────────────────────
-# Leave blank for no auth (fine behind a VPN). Format: "key:tenant,key2:*"
-COMP_LENS_API_KEYS=
+# ─── API auth (required when APP_ENV=production) ──────────────────
+# Format: "key:tenant,key2:*"  —  ':*' grants access to every tenant.
+# The key below was auto-generated for you; send it as the X-API-Key header.
+# Add more entries separated by ';' to scope keys to individual tenants.
+COMP_LENS_API_KEYS=${ADMIN_KEY}:*
 
 # ─── Optional: activate live connectors ───────────────────────────
 # Only connectors listed here make real API calls. e.g. OKTA,GITHUB,AWS
@@ -102,6 +109,18 @@ ENVEOF
   ok "Wrote $ENV_FILE with generated secrets (mode 600)"
 fi
 
+# The admin key lives in .env whether we just wrote it or it already existed.
+# Read it back so step 5 can print it (and so we can smoke-test an authed call).
+ADMIN_KEY_LINE="$(grep -E '^COMP_LENS_API_KEYS=' "$ENV_FILE" | head -n1 | cut -d= -f2-)"
+ADMIN_KEY="${ADMIN_KEY_LINE%%:*}"
+
+if [ -z "${ADMIN_KEY_LINE}" ] && grep -qE '^APP_ENV=production' "$ENV_FILE"; then
+  warn "APP_ENV=production but COMP_LENS_API_KEYS is blank in $ENV_FILE."
+  say  "The app fails closed and will not start. Add a key, e.g.:"
+  say  "  COMP_LENS_API_KEYS=$(gen_secret):*"
+  die  "Fix $ENV_FILE and re-run ./install.sh"
+fi
+
 # ── 3. build + start ────────────────────────────────────────────────
 info "Building the application image (first run can take a few minutes)…"
 $COMPOSE build
@@ -138,8 +157,13 @@ fi
 
 printf "\n${c_green}${c_bold}Comp-Lens is running.${c_reset}\n\n"
 printf "  Dashboard   ${c_bold}http://%s:%s/dashboard${c_reset}\n" "$HOST_ADDR" "$HOST_PORT"
-printf "  API docs    http://%s:%s/docs\n" "$HOST_ADDR" "$HOST_PORT"
 printf "  Health      http://%s:%s/health/ready\n\n" "$HOST_ADDR" "$HOST_PORT"
+printf "Your admin API key (also in ${c_bold}.env${c_reset}, keep it secret):\n"
+printf "  ${c_bold}%s${c_reset}\n\n" "$ADMIN_KEY"
+printf "Send it on every API call:\n"
+printf "  curl -H 'X-API-Key: %s' http://%s:%s/summary\n\n" "$ADMIN_KEY" "$HOST_ADDR" "$HOST_PORT"
+printf "Interactive API docs are disabled in production. To enable them, set\n"
+printf "  ${c_bold}EXPOSE_API_DOCS=true${c_reset} in .env and re-run, then visit /docs\n\n"
 printf "Useful commands:\n"
 printf "  View logs       ${c_bold}%s logs -f app${c_reset}\n" "$COMPOSE"
 printf "  Stop            ${c_bold}%s down${c_reset}\n" "$COMPOSE"
