MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two POST handlers were registered on /v1/integrate/ai-systems/{system_id}/to-risk
with incompatible contracts: the first read tenant_id from the JSON body, the
second (documented, and consistent with every sibling /v1/integrate route) from
a query parameter. FastAPI matches the first registration, so callers passing
?tenant_id=acme were silently scoped to 'default' — a cross-tenant data bug in a
compliance product. Kept the query-parameter handler and taught it to accept the
body form too, so no existing caller breaks.

/v1/documents/ingest and /v1/documents/upload imported app.middleware_core and
app.services.middleware_service inside 'except Exception'. Neither module has
ever existed in this repository, so both endpoints always reported 'middleware
not available' while the broad except also hid any genuine failure. Replaced
with an explicit helper that states plainly that events are returned but not
stored, and dropped the now-unused DB session dependency from both handlers.

Also collapsed the duplicate import aliases the codegen workflows accumulated
(os as _os / _os_evm, FileResponse twice, BaseModel as _BaseModel / _PydBase),
and sourced the app version from app.__version__ instead of a literal.

