From 7d75bebdff7715a9a7ccc06a12c89677af78b93e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 18:54:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] refactor: fold the dead standalone control plane into the
 API
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

app/app.py was a second 198-line FastAPI application. Nothing imported it, no
Dockerfile or compose file ran it, and coverage reported it at 0% — yet it held
the only implementations of two endpoints the enforcement design depends on:
the OPA bundle at GET /enforcement/bundles/complens.tar.gz and the decision-log
sink at POST /enforcement/logs. Its bundle builder also called read_bytes()
unguarded, so an unprovisioned policy directory produced a 500 traceback.

Both endpoints now live in app.main on top of app.services.enforcement, which
already owned the read views and the ingestion core, so there is one
implementation of bundle_revision() instead of two that could disagree.
BundleNotProvisioned turns a missing bundle into a 503 with a message naming the
files it wants. The routes require an API key, which the standalone app did not.

The bundle directory itself is now real: POLICY_DIR defaulted to app/policy/,
which contains no main.rego and no data.json, so the whole feature was inert on
every deployment. main.rego moves to enforcement_policy/ alongside a data.json
and a README explaining the shadow/enforce switch, the Dockerfile copies it, and
the resolution order is ENFORCEMENT_POLICY_DIR then COMPLENS_POLICY_DIR — the
old name still works, and it is no longer confusable with POLICY_DIR, which
points at the unrelated YAML policy-as-code definitions.

Adds tests/test_enforcement_control_plane.py: 8 tests over bundle contents,
revision stability, gzip and plain decision logs, malformed-entry tolerance, and
the 503 path. Deletes the orphaned root compliance.rego.

The Dockerfile no longer installs gcc and libpq-dev: every dependency ships a
manylinux wheel, so they only inflated the runtime image and its CVE surface.
--only-binary=:all: makes a missing wheel fail the build loudly instead.

