From 740dfca9a9e5dcf55e462b49c9a5886fc9571aef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 18:54:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] fix: migrations had drifted 68 differences from the ORM
 models
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A database built the way production builds one — alembic upgrade head on an
empty file — did not match app/models.py. compare_metadata reported 68 pending
differences:

  * three declared indexes were never created
    (ix_evidence_documents_tenant_id, ix_evidence_concept_hits_tenant_id,
    ix_evidence_concept_hits_doc_id), so every tenant-scoped evidence-document
    query was a full table scan;
  * 65 columns declared NOT NULL in the models were nullable in the database,
    so the schema accepted rows the application assumes cannot exist.

Nothing caught this because the test suite builds its schema with
Base.metadata.create_all() and never executes a migration.

The new revision creates the indexes and tightens the constraints. Columns with
a server default are backfilled from it first so the migration is safe on a
populated database; columns without one are left to fail loudly, because a NULL
identifier or timestamp is real missing data that needs a decision rather than
an invented value. render_as_batch in alembic/env.py makes the ALTERs work on
SQLite and is a no-op on PostgreSQL, so one file covers both.

tests/test_migrations.py now runs alembic upgrade head into a temporary database
and asserts autogenerate finds nothing left to do, so a model change without a
migration fails CI instead of production. It also asserts the three indexes
exist and that the revision graph has exactly one head.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BX61MEYft2zHyTikPWZeGG
---
 alembic/env.py                                |   6 +-
 ...74dd62af38_align_schema_with_orm_models.py | 543 ++++++++++++++++++
 tests/test_migrations.py                      |  89 +++
 3 files changed, 637 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 alembic/versions/1e74dd62af38_align_schema_with_orm_models.py
 create mode 100644 tests/test_migrations.py

diff --git a/alembic/env.py b/alembic/env.py
index d5af8a5..eb1bcea 100644
--- a/alembic/env.py
+++ b/alembic/env.py
@@ -21,7 +21,11 @@ def run_migrations_online():
     from sqlalchemy import create_engine
     engine = create_engine(settings.database_url)
     with engine.connect() as conn:
-        context.configure(connection=conn, target_metadata=target_metadata)
+        # render_as_batch lets ALTER-heavy migrations (nullability, constraints)
+        # run on SQLite, which cannot ALTER COLUMN in place. It is a no-op on
+        # PostgreSQL, so a single migration file works on both backends.
+        context.configure(connection=conn, target_metadata=target_metadata,
+                          render_as_batch=True)
         with context.begin_transaction():
             context.run_migrations()
 
