From 6c4a8453781b0c2c0fd5660c199d0b43a4af52f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 18:54:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] chore: one config file, one version, and deployment
 manifests that agree with the code
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds pyproject.toml as the single tool-configuration file: project metadata,
pytest settings, and the ruff rules that lived in a separate ruff.toml (now
deleted). pytest's pythonpath and alembic.ini's prepend_sys_path replace the
PYTHONPATH=$GITHUB_WORKSPACE export CI needed, and 'addopts = -p no:randomly'
means test ordering no longer depends on every caller remembering the flag —
several modules share a database file, so random order would be flaky.

The version was a '1.2.0' literal in main.py while the README and ruff config
called the project '2.0'. app.__version__ is now the single source and both
pyproject.toml and the OpenAPI schema read from it.

render.yaml, the only deployment manifest in the repo, set
ENABLE_DEMO_CONNECTOR=true in production. The DEMO connector fabricates 'pass'
evidence, and app/config.py defaults it off in production specifically so nobody
can manufacture a clean compliance record — the manifest was overriding that
guarantee. Set to false. It also never set TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS, which config.py's
own comment says should be 1 behind Render; without it every anonymous caller
shares one rate-limit bucket keyed on the proxy's IP.

CI drops COMP_LENS_SECRET_KEY, which no code has ever read, and gains a
container-build job that asserts the dashboard HTML, the framework JSON data,
the enforcement bundle and the YAML policies are all actually present in the
image — .dockerignore excludes *.html and *.json, and while those patterns are
root-anchored today, nothing was checking. .dockerignore now says so explicitly.
.gitignore picks up test_v16_ev/, the 344 KB of evidence artifacts the suite
writes into the repository root on every run.

